From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] soc: samsung: the G3D body bias logs its routine
 transitions at debug level

pd_g3d powers on and off several times a second while the GPU works: a
2-hour soak at 160 to 700 MHz counted 9800 power-offs.  The driver
logged every BB_CON4 write at info level, rate limited, which kept the
kernel log busy with nothing worth reading.

Log the routine transitions with dev_dbg; the debugfs file still counts
them (power_on_count, power_off_count).  A value this driver did not
leave in BB_CON4, written by something else, still gets a line of its
own, a rate-limited warning, since it means someone else programs the
G3D body bias.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/soc/samsung/exynos5433-g3d-abb.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos5433-g3d-abb.c b/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos5433-g3d-abb.c
index b92010bc0..7e89d0080 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos5433-g3d-abb.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos5433-g3d-abb.c
@@ -78,11 +78,21 @@ static int g3d_abb_set(struct g3d_abb *abb, u32 val, const char *why)
 
 	regmap_read(abb->pmu, EXYNOS5433_PMU_BB_CON4, &old);
 	ret = regmap_write(abb->pmu, EXYNOS5433_PMU_BB_CON4, val);
+	/*
+	 * The domain powers on and off several times a second while the GPU
+	 * works (9800 power-offs in a 2-hour soak), so the routine transitions
+	 * are debug lines; the debugfs file counts them.  Only a value this
+	 * driver did not leave there, written by something else, is worth a
+	 * line of its own.
+	 */
 	if (ret)
 		dev_err(abb->dev, "%s: cannot write BB_CON4: %d\n", why, ret);
-	else
-		dev_info_ratelimited(abb->dev, "%s: BB_CON4 0x%08x -> 0x%08x\n",
+	else if (old != abb->on_val && old != abb->off_val)
+		dev_warn_ratelimited(abb->dev,
+				     "%s: BB_CON4 was 0x%08x, not a level of this driver; now 0x%08x\n",
 				     why, old, val);
+	else
+		dev_dbg(abb->dev, "%s: BB_CON4 0x%08x -> 0x%08x\n", why, old, val);
 	return ret;
 }
 
